    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line via the logger named `AUDIT` on successful owner creation, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n`POST /api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (V2 only serves the paged list). I made three edits to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. Added SLF4J `Logger`/`LoggerFactory` imports.\n2. Declared a static `AUDIT` logger: `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n3. Immediately after the successful `saveOwner(owner)` call (which populates the generated id), emitted:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nPlacing the log after `saveOwner` (and after all the reject-path early returns) ensures it only fires on a genuinely successful create, and that the id is present. The `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test \u2014 which captures the `AUDIT` Logback logger and asserts the line contains the id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` \u2014 passes, as does the full suite.",
